SUMMARY:Deadline: Loeb Fellowship 2027-28 at Harvard Graduate School of Des
 ign
DESCRIPTION:The Loeb Fellowship at Harvard Graduate School of Design is a y
 ear-long residential fellowship for accomplished mid-career practitioners 
 shaping the built and natural environment: urban designers\, public artist
 s\, architects\, landscape architects\, urban planners\, developers\, jour
 nalists\, civic leaders\, policymakers and community development leaders (
 past fellows have included a theater director\,...\n\nOrganisation: Harvar
 d Graduate School of Design\nLocation: Harvard Graduate School of Design\,
  Cambridge\, Massachusetts\, US. Open internationally\; fellows must remai
 n in residence in the Cambridge area while classes are in session (J-1 vis
 a for international fellows).\nAward: Stipend of USD 57\,500 for the acade
 mic year (taxable)\, plus housing for fellows and their families coming fr
 om outside the Boston/Cambridge area through 30 June\, and a travel grant 
 covering approximately one economy round trip home per semester. No applic
